;   See below for example implementations.
;
;   - [cam_anim] is the animation to be played.
;       + It can be any integer number from 1 to 5.
;           - Anim #1 is a 1 frame flick. (2000RPM ~ infinity)
;           - Anim #2 is a blazing fast flick. (1800RPM ~ 2000RPM)
;           - Anim #3 is a really fast flick. (1400RPM ~ 1800RPM)
;           - Anim #4 is the "fast" flick. (800RPM ~ 1400RPM)
;           - Anim #5 is the "normal" flick. (1RPM ~ 800RPM)
;       + Anims 1, 2, and 3 should be avoided if possible because they can be super disorienting.
;       + Automatically adjusted in the script depending on current RPM, can be forced by setting [force_cam] to true in the profile.
;
;   - [cam_shake] are the screen shake and roll effects.
;       + [cam_shake] needs to have 3 values registered separated by a comma.
;       + These values can be any float number from 0 into maybe positive infinite.
;       + First value controls horizontal screen shake.
;       + Second value controls vertical screen shake.
;       + Third value controls screen roll.
;       + These effects always use a random direction (i.e.: left or right at random).
;       + These effects always use an animation that's 2 grades faster (i.e.: If anim #5 is chosen, then shakes will be anim #3)
;
;   - [cam_recoil] are the, you know, recoil values.
;       + [cam_recoil] needs to have 2 values registered separated by a comma.
;       + These values can be any float number from 0 into maybe positive infinite.
;       + Every value in [cam_recoil] can have an additional property appended to them with a : (i.e.: 1.0:1)
;           - Not specifying this bit means that the direction of the animation will be random.
;       + First value controls horizontal recoil, :0 turns the camera to the right, :1 to the left.
;       + Second value controls vertical recoil, :0 turns the camera upwards, :1 downwards.
;       + 1.455815984859513757461056922405 is EXACTLY 1 degree.
;
;   - You can define spray patterns (think: CS:GO, old Rust, etc.) by using [e_(shot index)], see below for a pattern example implementation.
;
;   - [cam_fov] is an FOV pull effect.
;       + This effect can be any value from 0.0 into maybe positive infinite.
;       + This effect always use an animation that's 2 grades faster (i.e.: If anim #5 is chosen, then shakes will be anim #3)
;       + Due to X-Ray weirdness, you should NEVER go overboard on this unless the weapon shoots slowly, because you WILL glitch your camera into geometry, making your shots hit the wall behind you.
;
;   - [gun_shake_k] is the modifier for how much the viewmodel moves from the recoil shake and roll effects.
;       + A negative value means that the weapon will shake in the opposite direction to the camera (I think this looks better).
;
;   - [max_recoil] (+1) is the max divisor for recoil intensity. [-0.999(...) .. inf+]
;       + For positives || i.e.: max_recoil = 2.00 >> (recoil / (1.0 + 2.00)) = recoil / 3.0
;       +               ||       max_recoil = 8.00 >> (recoil / (1.0 + 8.00)) = recoil / 9.0
;       + For negatives || i.e.: max_recoil = -0.5 >> (recoil / (1.0 + -0.5)) = recoil / 0.5 = recoil * 2.0
;       +               ||       max_recoil = -0.9 >> (recoil / (1.0 + -0.9)) = recoil / 0.1 = recoil * 10.0
;       +               ||       max_recoil = -0.995 >> (recoil / (1.0 + -0.995)) = recoil / 0.005 = recoil * 200.0
;   - [max_shots] is the amount of consecutive shots needed to reach [max_recoil], a sine curve is used for the divisor before reaching [max_shots].
;       + Check [https://www.desmos.com/calculator/7ipcqgso65] to see how the sine curve for your settings look. Replace [a] with max_recoil, and [b] with max_shots.
;
;   - Other modifiers
;       + [hburst_k]        --> Scales the hyperburst recoil reduction intensity. [0..1] Default: 1.0 
;       + [variance_k]      --> Scales the 17.5% (see random_offset in the script) random recoil offset. [0..1] Default: 1.0
;       + [h_max_r_k]       --> Scales the max recoil divisor for horizontal specifically. [0..1] Default: 1.0
;       + [h_var_k]         --> Scales the 17.5% (see random_offset in the script) random recoil offset for horizontal specifically. [0..1] Default: 1.0
;       + [cam_return]      --> Makes recoil return to the origin spot like in Recoil: GOLD, make sure to adjust max_recoil accordingly. bool Default: false
;       + [reset_k]         --> Scales the time (2.5x cycle time) to reset the consecutive shot counter. [0.1 .. 10] Default: 1.0
;       + [force_norm]      --> Forces regular recoil progression for a profile if the "Reverse recoil scaling" MCM option is enabled. bool Default: false
;       + [force_cam]       --> Forces the profile's defined cam_anim instead of adjusting based on RPM. bool Default: false
;
;   - [postprocess] are additional fluff Post Process Effects.
;       + These can be black, blur, duality_h, duality_v, grey
;           - NOTE: Blur seems to be broken (blame Anomaly), but you can "create" a blur by using both duality_h and duality_v together.
;       + These are listed as: effect=strength, effect2=strength
;       + Strengths are always static and go from 0.0 to 1.0.
;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;
;   - Design tips for your own profiles:
;       + Cam anim #4 should be used mostly by SMGs or really fast shooting weapons.
;       + Shake, roll, and the FOV pull are designed by default to be tied to the default caliber the gun uses.
;           - Roll is designed by default to be 0.5x the shake as to prevent motion sickness.
;       + Try to avoid not specifying a direction for horizontal recoil to allow the player to be fully in control, otherwise, try to keep the horizontal recoil really low, like 0.5 and lower.
;       + For weapons that have a foregrip, try setting [variance_k] to a lower value, this results in less random recoil.
;       + For weapons that have a muzzle brake, try settings [max_recoil] to a higher value and (hear me out) [h_max_r_k] to a LOWER value, this would result in a higher max divisor for vertical recoil, and a lower max divisor for horizontal. 
;       + Anims 1, 2, and 3 are extremely fast, disorienting, and look bad for recoil. Try to not use them.
;           - If you REALLY need to use them, try using anim #3 for weapons that cycle faster than 1600RPM. Yes, this means that the other 2 have no actual use cases.
;       + For the looped shot in patterns, try setting both horizontal and vertical recoil to a high number without specifying a direction.
;       + For the duality_ Post Process Effects, try using values below 0.015 unless it's a slow firing weapon, as the effect ramps up really violently.
;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;;  [example_implementation]:base_recoil, 5.56x45   ;; Make sure to ALWAYS inherit from [base_recoil], otherwise make sure to provide all fields in your section. This profile will use some defaults from the 5.56x45 effects.
;;      cam_anim    = 5                             ;; Animation #5 will be used as a base.
;;      cam_shake   = 1.0, 1.0, 0.5                 ;; Mild screen shake and roll.
;;      cam_recoil  = 1.0, 5.0:0                    ;; Mild random direction horizontal recoil, strong upwards vertical recoil.
;;      cam_fov     = 10.0                          ;; Mild FOV pull.
;;      gun_shake_k = -0.15                         ;; Viewmodel will move for 15% of the cam_shake values.
;;      max_recoil  = 2.0                           ;; Recoil intensity will climb down to 33% (divided by (1.0 + 2.0)) of its initial value.
;;      max_shots   = 5                             ;; And will do so over the course of the first 5 consecutive shots.
;;      h_max_r_k   = 0.5                           ;; Horizontal recoil max divisor will climb up to 2.0 (1.0 + (max_recoil * h_max_r_k)) instead of 3.0.
;;      postprocess = duality_h=0.1, duality_v=0.1  ;; Extremely strong blur effect.

;;  [example_pattern_implementation]
;;      e_1     = 0.25:0, 1.5:0                     ;;  Shot index #1
;;      e_2     = 0.75:0, 2.5:0                     ;;  Shot index #2
;;      e_3     = 1.5:0, 3.0:0                      ;;  Shot index #3
;;      e_4     = 1.0:0, 3.25:0                     ;;  Shot index #4
;;      [...]
;;      e_31    = 2.0, 2.0                          ;; If no more indexes are defined, the pattern will loop on the last one, in this case it's index #31.
;;
;;  ![example_implementation]:example_pattern_implementation        ;; Now the pattern is hooked to a profile.


[cam_anim_1]
    frames_peak     = 1.56                          ;; Looks terrible (1.6 is somehow super precise 100fps)

[cam_anim_2]
    frames_peak     = 1.56                          ;; This one also looks terrible

[cam_anim_3]
    frames_peak     = 1.69

[cam_anim_4]
    frames_peak     = 2.5

[cam_anim_5]
    frames_peak     = 3

[base_recoil]
    cam_anim    = 5                                 ;; Pick one of the 5 cam_anim_ sections
    cam_shake   = 0.5, 0.5, 0.25                    ;; Horizontal shake, vertical shake, camera roll
    cam_recoil  = 0.5, 1.0:0                        ;; Horizontal recoil, vertical recoil
    cam_fov     = 1.0                               ;; How far back to pull the camera 
    gun_shake_k = -0.1                              ;; Gun movement coefficient -- (cam_shake * gun_shake_k)
    max_recoil  = 1.0                               ;; Max recoil divisor -- (1 + max_recoil)
    max_shots   = 1                                 ;; Consecutive shots needed to reach max_recoil
    hburst_k    = 1.0                               ;; Neutral misc. modifiers
    variance_k  = 1.0
    h_max_r_k   = 1.0
    h_var_k     = 1.0
    cam_return  = false                             ;; Disable GOLD's recoil auto reset "feature" by default
    reset_k     = 1.0
    force_norm  = false
    force_cam   = false
    postprocess =                                   ;; No default post process effects

